comments[73]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T09:07:30.168Z",codex-agent,Planning only. Implementation is deferred until the current delivery is reviewed.
  "2026-10-21T04:41:10.473Z",codex-agent,"Scope extended to published pm-cli 2026.10.21 as requested. Compare both releases against the October 19 native slice; implement applicable deltas, prove fail-before/pass-after behaviour, and require all four coverage dimensions plus the three-platform gates. No-git acceptance will require every real process write and history record to survive."
  "2026-10-21T04:47:20.325Z",codex-agent,"Implementation covers conservative same-host original-process death receipts and recovery intent, strict serialized mutation keys, invocation-preserving lock advice, effective default ordering, count-based completion rounding, and cursor page-local blocker focus. Test execution remains outside the native slice and unsupported run options are preflight-refused before linked-test edits. Assurance declaration reads gain typed missing-ID refusals and bounded read-only discovery."
  "2026-10-21T04:59:54.507Z",codex-agent,"The updated library pass reports 285 tests passed. Focused admission tests additionally cover every submitted concurrency mutation, dead-owner recovery audit failure, unknown serialized options, read-only assurance refusals against the oracle, and a poison Git executable proving plain-directory linked tests never launch Git. Remaining work: complete differential/gate runs, behavioural reversion and exact-head three-platform CI."
  "2026-10-21T05:07:07.453Z",codex-agent,"The strengthened real-process test exposed a genuine owner-release race: a process can release its observed lock and exit between owner inspection and stale-lock reread. Early recovery then surfaced a vanished lock as a fatal filesystem error. Treat vanished/pending-delete reread and unlink observations as bounded contention, retain structural faults, and require deterministic regression plus all 24 accepted writes and 25 history records."
  "2026-10-21T05:13:41.091Z",codex-agent,"Real-process plain-directory acceptance now passes: all 24 submitted comments survive exactly once, all 25 history entries remain, and every hash-chain link agrees. The vanished-owner reread/unlink race is retryable contention. Six focused parity scenarios also passed; final scoped-retry refinement, behavioural revert proofs, full coverage and exact-head three-platform CI remain pending."
  "2026-10-21T05:21:20.718Z",codex-agent,Initial macOS and Windows jobs found six future-clock lock tests that incorrectly expected Linux process liveness. Unsupported hosts must report unknown while retaining every original lock/item/history byte; expected diagnostics now reflect that boundary. Preserve valid tokenless owner receipts as the published parser does. Linux library coverage preview passed 287 tests; full-scope four-dimension coverage remains a separate gate.
  "2026-10-21T05:28:36.261Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: reverting changed production behaviour made five of six process scenarios fail, eight library checks fail, and the cursor recovery formatter fail. The original context fixture could hide leaked rows through per-section limits; a mixed Feature/Task fixture now fails separately when only the packing predicate is reverted. All production files were restored. Differential CLI fixtures now use equal cwd-based invocations on both sides; explicit workspace recovery is independently asserted rather than normalized away. Added real Git branch and missing-executable provenance cases plus assurance error propagation checks."
  "2026-10-21T05:37:55.250Z",codex-agent,"Corrected a missing filesystem qualifier in the new provenance fixture. Strict all-target Clippy now passes, and the targeted real-Git/missing-executable provenance test passes with exactly one selected test and both child modes asserted. Added explicit safety-contract rustdoc to every new process and identity test. The next aggregate uses a fresh home with global and system Git configuration disabled; earlier refusals/failures are not gate approvals."
  "2026-10-21T05:54:17.483Z",codex-agent,"Oracle differential found an additional literal-value delta: close recovery now preserves whitespace and empty arguments instead of trimming or dropping them. The new formatter regression failed before the fix and passes afterward. A 50-declaration probe also exposed an advertised but unaccepted output cursor; native assurance now accepts snapshot continuation and row caps. Its regression failed before the fix, then passed a complete unique-row walk, read-only byte check and stale-snapshot refusal. Strict all-target Clippy passes after both changes."
  "2026-10-21T06:04:32.845Z",codex-agent,"All 27 CLI unit tests now pass. Updated the legacy close-refusal expectation to the oracle literal whitespace value rather than the following option token; the exact comparison remains. Supplemental closure and bounded-assurance before/after tests pass, and the 50-row read remains byte-preserving."
  "2026-10-21T06:13:39.533Z",codex-agent,"The pm-managed focused acceptance now passes after clearing inherited tracker context inside process fixtures: 1 concurrency test plus 7 parity tests, all real processes. The concurrency case accepts all 24 writes and validates 25 chained history records. CI next exposed obsolete list golden envelopes; both implementations agree on the new priority and effective sorting fields, so the fixed-clock goldens are being refreshed directly from the pinned published oracle."
  "2026-10-21T06:16:52.175Z",codex-agent,All 8 list differential tests pass after regenerating all 11 fixed-clock golden envelopes directly from pm-cli 2026.10.21. macOS and Windows strict Clippy found the new oracle lock-tool helper was compiled outside its Linux-only caller; scoped the helper to Linux instead of suppressing warnings. Full aggregate and platform certification remain pending.
  "2026-10-21T06:25:27.066Z",codex-agent,Linux functional CI reached the mutation contract and found a pre-update ownerless-lock assertion. The pinned oracle now explicitly reports owner process unknown with reason lock_owner_unknown. The focused updated contract passes (1 selected test); item/history byte checks remain intact. Running the later read-contract suites with no-fail-fast to collect downstream oracle differences before the next CI push.
  "2026-10-21T06:34:56.807Z",codex-agent,"The downstream context differential exposed another applicable rendering delta: published TOON preserves explicit nulls and empty descendants inside object rows while compacting envelope metadata. The pre-fix deep blocked-fallback comparison fails on those missing facts. Implemented the same recursive boundary and added an independent fixed wire example captured from the pinned formatter; post-fix unit/differential verification is running. Stopped the older aggregate because its production code changed during the run; it is diagnostic only."
  "2026-10-21T06:54:56.002Z",codex-agent,"The broader oracle run exposed supported read deltas beyond the initial release examples: compact brief-list JSON and byte estimates, partial brief TOON disclosure, hidden row-contract suppression in dependency costs, and typed rendered-budget recovery replacing oversized packet success. Implementing the published bounded feasibility search, canonical retry preservation and actual retry replay. Existing tests that asserted oversized success are being updated to the new usage refusal and bounded-delivery contract. No gate thresholds or source exclusions changed."
  "2026-10-21T07:06:41.750Z",codex-agent,"Updated read contracts pass all 295 library tests and all 29 CLI unit tests. This includes real cursor-preserving budget retries, explicit traversal controls, summary-budget refusal, cost-limited fallback, compact JSON byte spelling, partial/unchecked brief envelopes, and lossless TOON row facts. Strict lint and exact process differentials are running; full coverage and latest-head three-platform CI are still required."
  "2026-10-21T07:12:45.004Z",codex-agent,"Strict all-target Clippy passed after the bounded-read implementation. CI then caught formatting in the final encoding-precedence helper, which was added after the earlier formatting pass. Regenerating formatting and requiring a fresh fmt check before the next push; this CI result is a failure, not certification."
  "2026-10-21T07:30:43.706Z",codex-agent,"Exact process acceptance now passes the relationship refusal matrix, the advertised canonical retry replay in both CLIs, bounded-list byte receipts, and collection safety refusals. CI narrowed orientation to one legacy depends_on resolution gap; fixed alias/sentinel handling, and preserved empty/whitespace search recovery arguments. Strict Clippy passes. All 297 library tests and all 31 CLI unit tests pass. The coverage preview exposed duplicated generic search instantiations and untested classification paths; use one borrowed probe implementation and explicit refusal-boundary checks. Full coverage and platform certification remain pending."
  "2026-10-21T07:39:28.165Z",codex-agent,"The complete context-sections differential now passes after legacy depends_on resolution. The full search-refusal matrix also passes after retaining literal empty/whitespace normalized arguments and rejected option values. All 31 CLI unit tests pass. These are exact stdout/stderr/status comparisons; no output normalization or threshold reductions were introduced. Next: behavioral revert proofs for the additional read changes, then the unchanged aggregate and platform coverage gates."
  "2026-10-21T07:43:47.213Z",codex-agent,"Additional behavioral revert proof completed: seven selected runs produced eight intended test failures for partial brief projection, row-fact preservation, compact JSON, typed packet recovery, legacy blocker resolution, literal search arguments, rejected values and rendered packet cost. No compile failures counted as proofs. All six production files were restored byte-for-byte. Starting the unchanged full pm-managed release-check with a fresh home and global/system Git configuration disabled."
  "2026-10-21T08:02:43.674Z",codex-agent,"All three complete functional and latency matrix jobs passed. Linux aggregate measured 100% functions, 99.964% lines, 99.944% regions and 99.789% branches; the unchanged 100% gate correctly refused certification. Adding focused command-refusal encoding, cursor-recovery and newline-error tests, and simplifying the equivalent durable receipt I/O chain. Full aggregate verification remains pending."
  "2026-10-21T08:07:16.979Z",codex-agent,"The Windows aggregate additionally exposed a native executable stack overflow in the instrumented create path; normal Windows tests passed. Added an MSVC-only executable stack reserve of 8 MiB, leaving committed pages demand-grown and all test/coverage gates intact. Focused refusal rendering tests now exercise human unknown-error fallback, explicit JSON, scoped cursor recovery and newline I/O failure. The superseded local aggregate was stopped after source changes; it is not counted as a pass."
  "2026-10-21T08:39:07.816Z",codex-agent,"Current functional suites passed with 558 Linux, 548 macOS and 542 Windows tests, zero failures or ignored cases. The macOS aggregate then identified four branch outcomes and two regions confined to CLI refusal handling. Added exclusive-flag and bare-cursor recovery cases, consolidated duplicate unknown-error routing, and added a real-process completion-overflow regression for human/JSON encoding and unchanged item/history bytes. The old local aggregate was stopped after test changes; no aggregate pass is claimed. Windows context latency measured 257.375 ms against the unchanged 250 ms gate; an isolated rerun is pending workflow completion."
  "2026-10-21T08:43:52.729Z",codex-agent,"All three aggregate jobs completed normal and instrumented functional suites and reached the unchanged coverage guard with the same four branch and two region gaps in CLI refusals. The Windows native stack reserve is therefore verified against the prior stack-overflow failure. Latest focused instrumentation passes 32 CLI unit tests plus eight real-process parity tests, including completion overflow in both encodings without item/history changes. Preparing a fresh full aggregate on these final refusal checks; coverage certification and the isolated Windows latency rerun remain pending."
  "2026-10-21T09:22:10.813Z",codex-agent,"The latest Linux aggregate still reports three branch outcomes and two regions in the common CLI refusal formatter. The combined source view hid gaps in separately compiled unit/native instantiations. Reworked equivalent optional recovery-map handling and added actual CLI preflight coverage across context, search, test, close, claim, cursor and budget refusals; the new process acceptance passes and verifies unchanged item/history bytes. Checking each compiled formatter instantiation before another aggregate run. The superseded local aggregate was stopped; no 100 percent gate is claimed."
  "2026-10-21T09:25:35.074Z",codex-agent,"Clean focused instrumentation passed 32 CLI unit tests, 15 CLI process tests and eight parity process tests. All 12 compiled command-refusal formatter functions/closures executed; each has zero missed branch outcomes and zero missed regions, including both unit/native instances. Strict Clippy and all 15 CLI process tests also pass after splitting the test-case table. Full-source, three-platform aggregate certification remains pending; no source exclusions or threshold changes were introduced."
  "2026-10-21T09:44:43.777Z",codex-agent,"The fresh local aggregate failed one large-edge differential case when its native subprocess reached the existing five-second deadline under parallel test load. The identical isolated test passed all cases in 59.55 seconds with the deadline intact. Current Linux/macOS CI functional suites passed it as well. Rerunning the local aggregate with RUST_TEST_THREADS=1 to serialize independent cases; each scenario retains its internal process concurrency, every deadline and all coverage thresholds. The CI matrix recipe is unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T10:02:54.620Z",codex-agent,"The previous macOS aggregate narrowed the remaining CLI gaps to two startup-argument branch outcomes and one region. Added actual no-command, unsupported namespace, missing assurance operand, all scope alias and deterministically closed-stderr cases. Startup normalization now accepts the owned argument vector it already required, eliminating redundant generic instantiations. Clean focused instrumentation passed 32 CLI unit, 16 CLI process and eight parity process tests: all 22 compiled startup/refusal/error-writer functions and closures executed with zero missed branches or regions; both assurance dispatch instances are covered too. Latest strict Clippy and all 56 stable-toolchain tests pass. Restarting complete three-platform and serialized local aggregates; full-source 100 percent certification remains pending."
  "2026-10-21T11:01:38.832Z",codex-agent,"PR 101 review round: fetched all five unresolved threads with complete comments; latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Branch is current and contains main. Verify workspace aliases, one lock wait budget, tracker scope, environment isolation, and oracle receipt retention; add behavioral revert proofs and run unchanged just release-check."
  "2026-10-21T11:03:04.444Z",codex-agent,"Verified receipt cleanup against pinned pm-cli 2026.10.21: dist/core/lock/lock-gc.js runLockGc enumerates only direct locks entries ending in .lock; recordDeadLockRecovery writes locks/recoveries/*.json. Therefore upstream retains recovery receipts and no cleanup is added. Will capture an executable aged-receipt GC probe and document retained audit policy."
  "2026-10-21T11:06:48.793Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs completed: reverting only published_read_arguments fails published_refusal_arguments_strip_all_workspace_aliases; reverting only preserve_lock_scope fails lock_recovery_keeps_explicit_workspace_scope; reverting canonical item-deps normalization fails scoped_alias_refusals_match_the_native_command; restoring acquire_lock environment/settings reread fails resolved_zero_wait_budget_is_used_without_rereading_settings; restoring inherited Git config fails fixture_git_configuration_is_neutral; restoring only the old materialized body fails certification_tracker_body_matches_the_active_oracle. All six runs exited 101 with assertion failures, never compile failures. Every file was restored and no history record was edited. The actual pinned-oracle GC probe passed with an aged receipt unchanged and zero locks scanned/removed."
  "2026-10-21T11:08:53.607Z",codex-agent,"Stopped the previous same-worktree release-check that started before this review round; its coverage compile overlapped changed sources, so it is not certification evidence. Cleaned workspace coverage artifacts. Fresh pm-managed focused acceptance and release-check are running with a fresh home, neutral global/system Git config and RUST_TEST_THREADS=1. The first managed invocation was safely refused because pm-context none requires isolated/snapshot workspace mode; reran using the supported default schema context without changing configuration. No PM CLI bug was identified."
  "2026-10-21T11:09:43.560Z",codex-agent,"Restored-code pm-managed focused acceptance passed 359 tests: 298 library, 33 CLI unit, 17 CLI process and 11 parity process; zero failed or ignored. Formatting, strict all-target Clippy and private-item documentation passed in the fresh full release-check, which is now executing all tests. Existing history bytes remain an exact prefix. Pushing the review-fix candidate to start exact-head platform CI while the local aggregate continues."
  "2026-10-21T11:12:42.594Z",codex-agent,"Supplementary full tracker audit confirms only the pre-existing pm-rust-bj7a and pm-rust-unih chain mismatches; both item/history pairs are byte-identical to origin/main. Added evidence to existing follow-up pm-rust-b4yl, avoiding a duplicate. Clone-local merge-driver configuration was refreshed using the pinned merge install; no tracked configuration or history was repaired. Full history integrity remains an explicitly separate open risk."
  "2026-10-21T11:30:42.855Z",codex-agent,"Exact code-head ca04e80834831d82ec0cac807a40345d64743555 CI functional suites passed all 22 binaries per platform: Linux 567, macOS 557, Windows 551 tests, zero failed/ignored. CodeQL and all three latency jobs passed. Linux just release-check also passed both full runs (567 stable plus 567 instrumented): lines 13965/13965, functions 1458/1458, regions 23337/23337, branches 3288/3288, all exactly 100 percent at unchanged thresholds. Audit, changelog and clone-local default health passed in that job. macOS/Windows aggregates remain running; supplementary full history integrity is still separately blocked by existing pm-rust-b4yl."
  "2026-10-21T11:42:57.286Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round gate receipt at code head ca04e80834831d82ec0cac807a40345d64743555: all nine CI jobs and CodeQL passed. Full just release-check ran 44 test binaries per platform (22 stable plus 22 instrumented), with Linux 567+567, macOS 557+557, Windows 551+551 passed and zero failed/ignored. All four required dimensions are exactly 100 percent: Linux lines 13965, functions 1458, regions 23337, branches 3288; macOS lines 13883, functions 1446, regions 23197, branches 3250; Windows lines 13882, functions 1447, regions 23197, branches 3252; covered equals total throughout. Audit, changelog, default clone-local health and latency gates passed. The supplemental serialized local run was intentionally stopped after 17 completed binaries and 479 passing tests once complete CI certification was available; it is not counted as an aggregate pass. Existing history prefixes remain unchanged against main and the initial PR head. Final pending commit contains tracker evidence only; production and test trees remain identical to the certified code head. No review threads were replied to or resolved. Full history integrity remains the existing pm-rust-b4yl risk."
  "2026-10-21T12:05:48.062Z",codex-agent,"PR 101 new review round: remote head 94dab89 is current and contains main. Complete reviewThreads pagination contains one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uwOSW with one comment and no omitted comments. Latest substantive CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Verified inherited Git repository-location variables can redirect source_ref despite current_dir; isolate production provenance and fixture processes, add hostile-environment regression and behavioral revert proof, then run unchanged just release-check."
  "2026-10-21T12:07:42.707Z",codex-agent,"Thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uwOSW fixed: source_ref strips GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_INDEX_FILE, GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY, GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES, GIT_COMMON_DIR and GIT_NAMESPACE before symbolic-ref. Existing SDK source-context init and assertion children now use the shared isolated environment. Self-review examined the complete production PR diff and all Git subprocess call sites: source_ref is the sole production Git command, and the other newly added Git probe already isolates its environment. No further instance in the changed code."
  "2026-10-21T12:07:43.635Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib sdk_collection_git_source_ignores_hook_repository -- --nocapture exits 101 when only production environment removals are reverted: provenance is hook-branch instead of source-branch. The same command exits 101 when only source-context fixture isolation is reverted: the real source fixture reports null instead of source-branch after redirected initialization. Both failures are runtime assertions, not compile failures. Restored changes pass cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib sdk_collection_git_source -- --nocapture (2 passed, 0 failed/ignored); strict all-target Clippy passes."
  "2026-10-21T12:41:24.713Z",codex-agent,"Final Git-provenance review gate receipt at code head 724cff8663fbd5ae350e4ded744035868205fdfa: all nine CI jobs and CodeQL passed. Unchanged just release-check ran 44 binaries per platform (22 stable plus 22 instrumented): Linux 568+568, macOS 558+558, Windows 552+552 passed; zero failed or ignored. All four required coverage dimensions are exactly 100 percent, covered equals total: Linux lines 13974, functions 1458, regions 23337, branches 3288; macOS lines 13892, functions 1446, regions 23197, branches 3250; Windows lines 13891, functions 1447, regions 23197, branches 3252. Formatting, strict Clippy, private documentation, dependency audit, changelog, default clone-local tracker health and all latency gates passed."
  "2026-10-21T12:41:26.270Z",codex-agent,"The supplemental fresh-home local aggregate with neutral Git config and RUST_TEST_THREADS=1 was intentionally stopped only after complete three-platform CI certification: 21 completed binaries, 551 passed and zero failed/ignored in completed binaries. It is not an aggregate pass; no timeout failure occurred this round. Separate full tracker health reconfirms only the existing pm-rust-bj7a and pm-rust-unih chain mismatches tracked by pm-rust-b4yl, with those item/history pairs unchanged from main. Existing history prefixes are preserved. Final evidence-only commit leaves certified production, test and build files unchanged. No thread replies/resolutions, merge or release were performed; claim is being released and item remains in progress."
  "2026-10-21T13:08:27.386Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched all three unresolved threads and every comment; pagination is complete. Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Remote head is current and includes origin/main. Verify lock identity, padded inverse blockers against the locked 2026.10.21 oracle, and optional-oracle test admission; add behavioral revert proofs, inspect the whole PR for matching cases, and run unchanged just release-check."
  "2026-10-21T13:14:02.489Z",codex-agent,"All three findings are valid. PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uxrCh: capture owner bytes and identity from the same open file; recheck dev/inode on Unix or native file identity on Windows before stale removal. Self-review also guards normal release and failed initialization cleanup against replacement files. PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uxrCr: the 2026.10.21 oracle resolves padded inverse blocks IDs; trim both sides and retain case-insensitive comparison. PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uxrDJ: use published_cli_or_skip for fixture setup and skip every oracle-dependent caller; required mode still fails closed. Whole production diff inspected for equivalent deletion, relationship normalization and optional-oracle admission patterns; no additional instances remain."
  "2026-10-21T13:14:05.040Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib stale_lock_replacement_with_identical_bytes_is_preserved fails with exit 101 and a runtime assertion when only remove_stale_lock identity checking is removed. The equivalent --lib released_lock_replacement_with_identical_bytes_is_preserved fails with exit 101 when only Drop identity checking is removed. cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --test orientation_differential padded_inverse_blockers_match_oracle fails with exit 101 and an exact stdout assertion when only inverse ID trimming is reverted. cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --test parity_1021_contract absent_oracle_obeys_optional_and_required_modes fails with exit 101 and a subprocess status assertion when only tracker oracle admission is reverted. Sources restored after each proof; no compile failure counted."
  "2026-10-21T13:14:53.743Z",codex-agent,"Fifth behavioral revert proof: cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib failed_lock_replacement_with_identical_bytes_is_preserved fails with exit 101 and the runtime assertion failed writer removed a replacement lock when only the failed-write cleanup identity guard is removed. Restored afterward. Read-only initialization failure still removes its own unchanged lock. The identity check narrows the pathname window under the existing lease; it is not an atomic compare-and-unlink against external writers that bypass the lease."
  "2026-10-21T13:17:26.341Z",codex-agent,"Restored PM-managed acceptance passed: three identity regressions, one exact 2026.10.21 blocker differential, and one optional/required oracle regression. The supplemental broad test run completed 302 library tests but its self-relaunch harness failed because an overlapping rebuild unlinked the running executable; the executable link confirmed the cause. Stopped that supplemental run and started the full unchanged aggregate without overlapping rebuilds, with a fresh home and neutral global/system Git configuration. No aggregate success is claimed until it completes."
  "2026-10-21T13:20:38.718Z",codex-agent,"Cross-platform self-review: snapshot Windows volume/file IDs rather than retaining owner handles, since retained handles can keep deletion pending and prevent immediate stale-lock recreation. Uses the already locked winapi-util version through a direct Windows-only dependency; no resolved package version changed. Existing forced-stale replacement with the original guard still alive covers immediate recreation on Windows. The local lock selector passed 25 tests; the previously affected self-relaunch harness passes alone. The aggregate was stopped before completion to restart on this correction; that partial run is not counted as a release pass."
  "2026-10-21T13:44:58.606Z",codex-agent,"The first macOS aggregate executed all 563 stable and 563 instrumented tests successfully, but the unchanged 100 percent region gate found two uncovered error-propagation regions in the new metadata helpers. Replaced nested question-mark propagation with Result mapping while preserving errors and file lifetime. Strict all-target Clippy passes. Instrumented library acceptance passes all 302 tests; the three identity helpers and both mapping closures have zero uncovered regions. The Windows clone result uses the same propagation form. No source exclusions or thresholds changed. All three standalone CI Rust suites and latency jobs passed; final aggregate recertification remains pending."
  "2026-10-21T14:15:57.883Z",codex-agent,"Final certification at code head c03335e826fb2edd392ca0eda51c0b74774cb849: all nine CI jobs passed in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39610776837 and CodeQL passed in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39610776769. The unchanged just release-check aggregate passes on Linux, macOS and Windows. Linux: 573 stable plus 573 instrumented tests; 14004/14004 lines, 1462/1462 functions, 23395/23395 regions, 3294/3294 branches. macOS: 563 plus 563 tests; 13922/13922 lines, 1450/1450 functions, 23254/23254 regions, 3256/3256 branches. Windows: 557 plus 557 tests; 13920/13920 lines, 1450/1450 functions, 23258/23258 regions, 3258/3258 branches. Each aggregate completed 44 binary executions with zero failed or ignored tests. All four required dimensions are exactly 100 percent with unchanged scope and thresholds. Fmt, strict Clippy, private rustdoc, identity, audit, changelog, clone-local health and all three latency gates passed. Audit retains the inherited allowed RUSTSEC-2024-0449 maintenance advisory."
  "2026-10-21T14:15:58.805Z",codex-agent,"Final review refetch confirms the same three unresolved thread IDs, all complete with no pagination gaps or new comments; the latest CodeRabbit review still has no outside-diff findings. All five restored PM-linked regressions pass on the certified source. A local parallel aggregate hit the existing five-second packet subprocess timeout; the exact isolated retry passed unchanged, and the scenario passed in the certified CI aggregates. Earlier stopped supplemental runs are not aggregate passes. Original history remains an unchanged byte prefix; only records were appended. Existing full-history follow-up pm-rust-b4yl remains out of scope, with no repair or re-anchoring. Default strict local health passed with three existing advisories. No new pm CLI or SDK defect was discovered. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; the item stays in progress. The final evidence commit changes only this item and its appended history; production, tests, build controls and documentation remain identical to the certified head."
  "2026-10-21T14:38:30.143Z",codex-agent,"PR #101 review round: fetched all four unresolved threads and every comment; pagination is complete. Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range section. Branch is current with remote and contains origin/main. Verify recovery-directory durability, single owner classification, optional oracle handling, and deterministic zero-wait regression; audit the whole PR for these classes, record behavioral revert proofs, and run unchanged just release-check."
  "2026-10-21T14:41:50.148Z",codex-agent,"Validated all four review findings. Recovery intent now flushes locks/recoveries and locks before stale unlink (including the newly created directory entry); diagnostics reuse one real owner observation, matching buildLockConflictError in the locked 2026.10.21 oracle; no-git concurrency honors optional and required oracle modes; zero-wait regression runs inline while holding the incumbent. Whole PR audit of publication, owner inspection, optional locator callers, and timing patterns found no further instance requiring an oracle divergence. Targeted tests pass; preparing isolated behavioral revert proofs."
  "2026-10-21T14:43:48.892Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: five isolated experiments each failed at runtime with exit 101 and restored fixed sources immediately. Reverting record_dead_owner produced zero directory flushes instead of two; removing only the new-directory parent flush produced one instead of two; reverting ownership_lock_refusal produced two real owner probes instead of one; reverting seeded_workspace and its concurrency caller made the absent optional oracle fail rather than skip; changing acquire_lock back to the configured wait budget made resolved_zero_wait_budget_is_used_without_rereading_settings violate its elapsed assertion after 2.04 seconds. Exact selectors and thread mapping are in docs/NATIVE_PARITY_2026_10_21.md. No oracle divergence requested or introduced."
  "2026-10-21T14:56:25.939Z",codex-agent,"All targeted regressions pass: three unit selectors and both concurrency contract tests. Strict Clippy and neutral-config tracker health pass; health retains three existing advisories. The full PM-linked just release-check is running with neutral Git configuration and a temporary HOME on a heavily contended four-CPU host. Push the reviewed code plus this tracker evidence to start dedicated CI while the local aggregate continues; no aggregate pass is claimed yet."
  "2026-10-21T15:06:27.199Z",codex-agent,"Pushed reviewed code head a88299be81c5430eef93fd3ec83a2ff7386f42e1. Automatic CI run 39621651104 is executing all three platform aggregates; CodeQL run 39621650870 is separate. GitHub PR metadata initially lagged the verified remote ref; it has caught up. The duplicate manual CI run was canceled and is not validation evidence. Refetched every unresolved thread and all comments at the new head: same four complete threads, no new comments, and no outside-diff findings. Local PM-linked aggregate remains active under heavy host contention. No aggregate result claimed yet."
  "2026-10-21T15:18:49.797Z",codex-agent,"At code head a88299be81c5430eef93fd3ec83a2ff7386f42e1, all standalone CI Rust suites pass: Linux 576 tests, macOS 565, Windows 559; each executes 22 test binaries with zero failed or ignored tests. All three latency jobs and CodeQL pass too. Three full just release-check aggregates remain active; standalone results do not substitute for their coverage/audit/changelog gates."
  "2026-10-21T15:27:36.176Z",codex-agent,"Linux CI ran all 576 stable and 576 instrumented tests successfully, but unchanged coverage correctly rejected one uncovered error-return region in record_dead_owner (23408 of 23409 regions). macOS aggregate passed at 100 percent in all four required dimensions. Added a deterministic real-filesystem race before the recovery-directory flush: retain the written audit under a different directory name, force the original-directory flush to fail, and verify the incumbent lock plus item/history bytes remain unchanged. The prior local aggregate was stopped as obsolete before this test expansion; it is not aggregate pass evidence. Validate the new failure branch and rerun gates without changing thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T15:31:59.546Z",codex-agent,"The expanded dead_owner_recovery_requires_a_durable_intent regression passes both directly and through pm test --run --only-last --progress with tracker/source context. Strict Clippy passes. Both macOS and Windows full aggregates pass at the first code head; Linux alone rejected the uncovered sync-error return after all 1152 test executions passed. The new thread-local test hook performs a real directory rename before sync, is absent from production builds, and makes the failure refusal deterministic while retaining audit evidence. Push this test expansion and rerun the full unchanged release gates; focused instrumentation is collecting the exact recovery-function region coverage."
  "2026-10-21T15:37:04.173Z",codex-agent,"Focused nightly branch instrumentation passes the expanded durable-intent case and reports zero uncovered code regions in record_dead_owner and its closures, including the previously missed error return. Sixth behavioral revert proof: omit only sync_parent(&receipt) while retaining the real directory-rename race. dead_owner_recovery_requires_a_durable_intent fails at runtime with exit 101 because acquisition is accepted instead of refusing the sync error. Restored committed source matches head 4c53da42ae0d9ce37a9a38a8443cd51fc2737369 and the regression passes again. Refetch at that head confirms the same four unresolved threads, all comments complete, with no outside-diff findings."
  "2026-10-21T15:53:14.388Z",codex-agent,"Replacement Linux just release-check passes at code head 4c53da42ae0d9ce37a9a38a8443cd51fc2737369: 576 stable plus 576 instrumented tests, 44 test-binary executions, zero failed or ignored tests. Required coverage is exactly 100 percent: lines 14011/14011, functions 1465/1465, regions 23414/23414, branches 3294/3294. The prior uncovered error-return region is closed with the real sync-failure regression; thresholds and source scope are unchanged. Main remains fully contained by the branch. Windows and macOS aggregates are still active. The separate macOS standalone job was canceled before runner allocation; GitHub refuses rerun until the workflow becomes terminal, so it is not counted as passed evidence."
  "2026-10-21T16:06:18.661Z",codex-agent,"All three unchanged just release-check aggregates pass at code head 4c53da42ae0d9ce37a9a38a8443cd51fc2737369 in CI run 39626582814. Linux: 576 stable + 576 instrumented tests; lines 14011/14011, functions 1465/1465, regions 23414/23414, branches 3294/3294. macOS: 565 + 565 tests; lines 13926/13926, functions 1452/1452, regions 23264/23264, branches 3256/3256. Windows: 559 + 559 tests; lines 13922/13922, functions 1451/1451, regions 23262/23262, branches 3258/3258. Each aggregate executes 44 test binaries, with zero failed or ignored tests and exactly 100 percent in all four required coverage dimensions. No thresholds or source exclusions changed. All latency jobs, CodeQL, and standalone Linux/Windows suites pass. The only separate missing CI job is macOS standalone, canceled before runner allocation; retry it now that the parent workflow is terminal. Original canceled/obsolete runs are not counted as passed evidence."
  "2026-10-21T16:21:15.644Z",codex-agent,"Final verification: CI run 39626582814 is fully green at certified code head 4c53da42ae0d9ce37a9a38a8443cd51fc2737369. The macOS standalone retry executed 22 binaries and passed all 565 tests, with zero failed or ignored tests; the original no-runner cancellation is not counted as a pass. All nine CI jobs and separate CodeQL now pass. Final review refetch confirms the same four unresolved threads, every comment read, no pagination gaps, and no outside-diff findings in the latest CodeRabbit body. All four findings are valid and fixed; six behavioral reverts fail at runtime with exit 101 and restored regressions pass. No oracle divergence, thread reply, resolution, merge, release, or new pm CLI/SDK defect. Existing full-history investigation pm-rust-b4yl remains out of scope; history was not repaired or re-anchored. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification while leaving this item in progress. The final evidence commit changes only this item and its appended history; source, tests, build controls and documentation remain identical to the certified head."
  "2026-10-21T16:49:10.968Z",codex-agent,"PR 101 review round: fetched all review threads and their complete comment pages; one remains unresolved, PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6u3EZE. Latest substantive CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Remote branch is current and contains origin/main. Will reproduce the pinned 2026.10.21 oracle before accepting the requested retry scope rewrite, self-review the full diff for related classes, and run the unchanged Rust release gate."
  "2026-10-21T16:53:15.373Z",codex-agent,"Oracle reproduction with a valid unexpired incumbent lock returns exit 4 for both explicit workspace and tracker directories. Published pm-cli 2026.10.21 preserves the literal supplied --pm-path in attempted_command, normalized_args, suggested_retry, suggested_retry_args and examples; it does not append .agents/pm. Therefore refuse PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6u3EZE as an oracle divergence. An initial malformed receipt was automatically reclaimed by the oracle, so the final reproduction uses a well-formed live-owner receipt. Self-review also found published comment retries canonicalize to item comments; native direct-comment retry advice needs the same normalization and executable replay acceptance. Adding a no-git differential over absolute and relative paths with spaces and all three native scope aliases in split and equals forms."
  "2026-10-21T17:03:13.864Z",codex-agent,"Three isolated behavioral proofs complete, all runtime exit 101 with successful builds and sources restored after each: reverting only ownership_error_json fails explicit_lock_retry_scopes_match_oracle because comment differs from oracle item comments; reverting only native_arguments fails canonical_comment_retry_arguments_are_accepted because the advertised namespace is rejected; applying only the requested preserve_lock_scope discovery rewrite fails the differential because .agents/pm is appended where the oracle preserves the supplied workspace. Before these experiments, both targeted regressions and the PM-linked differential passed; strict Clippy passed after two assignment-style corrections. The final implementation needs only the advice formatter and startup parser changes. Full diff self-review found no further valid instance in the inspected classes. Run the unchanged aggregate with neutral Git configuration next."
  "2026-10-21T17:09:23.065Z",codex-agent,"Pushed code and review evidence as 0029cf2e22e247b0cb806cf12a7dc6f022351482. The unchanged just release-check aggregate is running with a temporary home, neutral Git configuration and RUST_TEST_THREADS=1; concurrency scenarios retain their internal concurrent writers. Formatting, strict Clippy, private-item documentation and strict check-only tracker health pass. Health has three existing advisories and omits full history drift, so this is not a full-history integrity claim. One health invocation overlapped oracle reinstall and saw a transient missing module; the post-install retry passed. No aggregate pass is claimed yet."
  "2026-10-21T17:21:56.681Z",codex-agent,"At code head 0029cf2e22e247b0cb806cf12a7dc6f022351482, macOS standalone CI passes 567 tests across 22 binaries, with zero failed or ignored tests. All three latency jobs pass. Local completed library, CLI unit and branch-merge suites pass 339 tests; subsequent claim/release cases are progressing with no failures so far. Full aggregates remain pending and these partial or standalone results are not aggregate certification. Review refetch confirms the same one unresolved thread, complete comments and no outside-diff findings."
